---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";
---
<Layout title="College student healthcare in Blacksburg | Kin & Campus" description="A membership-based health program for college students in Blacksburg, with a local board-certified pediatrician coordinating ongoing care through the academic year.">
<div class="w hero2"><div><div class="eyebrow">College health in Blacksburg</div><h1>Good healthcare should continue when college begins.</h1><p class="lead">Kin &amp; Campus is a membership-based health program for college students in Blacksburg. A local, board-certified pediatrician coordinates the care they already rely on, sees them for common illnesses, and helps them learn how to manage their health with greater confidence each year.</p><p class="hero-cta"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Start a conversation</a><a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>Information for parents &rarr;</a><a class="lnk" href={href("students")}>Information for students &rarr;</a></p></div>
<img class="art" src={href("photos/drillfield-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="Fall leaves on the Drillfield, with Burruss Hall across the green">
</div>
<div class="w"><div class="trust"><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg><b>Ongoing care in one place</b><span>Follow-up for ADHD medication, asthma, anxiety and depression medication, allergies, acne, and other established needs.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><b>Care that follows the school year</b><span>Planned conversations around move-in, breaks, finals, and other points when routines and medications can change.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg><b>Clear communication</b><span>Parents are included with the student's consent, and the hometown physician is updated when clinically appropriate.</span></div></div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><div><div class="eyebrow">A local physician</div><h2>Someone in Blacksburg who knows the full picture.</h2><p>College students often need more than a one-time appointment. A refill may depend on regular follow-up. A cough means something different for a student with asthma. A medication that worked in high school may need attention once sleep, meals, and schedules change.</p><p>Because Kin &amp; Campus knows the student over time, each visit begins with context. The goal is steady, well-coordinated care during the years when students are gradually taking more responsibility for it themselves.</p><p><a class="lnk" href={href("care")}>See the care we provide &rarr;</a></p></div>
<svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 600 190" role="img" aria-label="Parent, Kin and Campus, and student connected"><path d="M112 80Q190 10 265 66M335 66Q410 10 488 80" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="2 10" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="70" cy="82" r="42" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="70" cy="70" r="12" fill="#F6EFE4"/><path d="M46 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#F6EFE4"/><circle cx="530" cy="82" r="42" fill="#C9A24B"/><circle cx="530" cy="70" r="12" fill="#2A1A1E"/><path d="M506 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#2A1A1E"/><circle cx="300" cy="78" r="40" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M272 84L300 58 328 84v22H272z" fill="#FBF7F0" stroke="#6B2737" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="293" y="90" width="14" height="16" fill="#C9A24B"/><g font-family="DM Sans,sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle"><text x="70" y="150">Parent</text><text x="300" y="150">Kin &amp; Campus</text><text x="530" y="150">Student</text></g></svg></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">What students can bring to us</div><h2>Everyday needs and ongoing concerns are part of the same relationship.</h2>
<div class="notes">
<div class="note-row"><h3>Medication follow-up</h3><p>We review established treatment, arrange appropriate refills, and pay attention to how medication is working in the student's actual college routine.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Illness and forms</h3><p>Students can be evaluated for common illnesses and bring us university, housing, sports, travel, and immunization paperwork that requires clinical review.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Planned check-ins</h3><p>Useful points in the academic year give us a chance to address sleep, stress, symptoms, adherence, and upcoming prescription needs before they become urgent.</p></div>
<div class="note-row"><h3>Practical skills</h3><p>Students learn how to describe symptoms, request refills in time, schedule care, understand their treatment, and recognize when they need help.</p></div>
</div></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">How the relationship begins</div><h2>We start by understanding what your student needs.</h2>
<ol class="steps">
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div><h3>Have an introductory conversation</h3><p>A parent or student can contact us to learn how the program works and discuss whether it is a good fit. We do not collect medical details through this website.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div><h3>Meet in Blacksburg</h3><p>The student establishes care with the physician and reviews the history, current treatment, and priorities for the school year through the appropriate clinical process.</p></div></li>
<li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div><h3>Build routines that work</h3><p>From there, care continues through visits, medication follow-up, planned check-ins, and coordination with family and other physicians when permitted and useful.</p></div></li>
</ol></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Student privacy</div><h2>Students decide how parents are involved.</h2><p>Adult students control their health information. We discuss communication preferences at the beginning and follow the student's consent. When coordination with a hometown physician would support care, we handle that through the proper clinical channels. <a class="lnk2" href={href("privacy")}>Read about privacy and communication &rarr;</a></p></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><h2>A program designed for continuity.</h2><p class="lead">Membership supports an ongoing clinical relationship during the academic year. Access follows the practice's clinical schedule, while insurance, emergency care, specialists, and hospital services continue to serve their usual roles.</p><p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn" href={href("membership")}>Understand membership</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
